      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Retrograde dissection re-entry can cause pericardial trauma of sufficient degree to lead to the development of an auto-immune postpericardial injury syndrome. Clinical suspicion for this condition should be high in the event of fever, symptoms, pericardial/pleural effusion, and pleuritic chest pain following chronic total occlusion (CTO) Post cardiac injury syndromes (PCI)."},
